.TH DS 1 "2026-08-10" "ds" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ds \- create and manage local or remote tmux dev sessions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ds
.RI [ session ]
.RI [ @host ]
.br
.B ds
.B -l
.RI [ @host ]
.br
.B ds
.B -k
.RI [ session ]
.RI [ @host ]
.br
.B ds
.B --killall
.RI [ @host ]
.br
.B ds
.B --share
.RI [ session ]
.br
.B ds
.B --unshare
.RI [ session ]
.br
.B ds
.B init
.RI < bash | zsh >
.br
.B ds
.B resurrect save
.I file
.br
.B ds
.B resurrect begin
.br
.B ds
.B resurrect restore
.RI [ file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ds
creates tmux development sessions locally or on remote hosts. A session name
selects a profile; a suffix after the first dash is treated as an instance tag
when the prefix matches a known profile.
.PP
Profiles, connection methods, and share backends are plugin-based. Bundled
plugins live with the installation. User overrides live under
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ds
when
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is nonempty, or under
.I ~/.config/ds
otherwise.
The configuration paths below are relative to that directory.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -l ", " --list
List active ds-managed sessions.
.TP
.BR -k ", " --kill
Kill the named session, or the current session when run inside tmux without a
name.
.TP
.B --killall
Kill all ds-managed sessions.
.TP
.BI -c ", --connect " method
Override the connection method selected for a remote host.
.TP
.BI -L ", --forward " local:remote
Add an SSH local port forward for a remote session.
.TP
.BI -R ", --reverse " remote:local
Add an SSH reverse port forward for a remote session.
.TP
.B --share
Share the named or current session.
.TP
.B --unshare
Stop sharing the named or current session.
.TP
.BI --share-via " backend"
Create or attach to the session and share it through the selected backend.
.TP
.B --no-attach
Create or update the session without attaching.
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Show usage.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.TP
.I profile-<name>.sh
User profile scripts. A profile script defines
.BI _profile_ name ()
and receives the session name.
.TP
.I profile*.conf
Data-only profile rows for single-command profiles.
.TP
.I connect*.conf
Host-to-connection-method rules. Files are additive and read in order.
.TP
.I connect-<method>.sh
User connection method plugins.
.TP
.I share-<backend>.sh
User share backend plugins.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Absolute base directory for user configuration. When unset, empty, or relative, defaults to
.IR ~/.config .
.TP
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
Absolute base directory for runtime state. When unset, empty, or relative,
defaults to
.IR ~/.local/state .
.TP
.B DS_STATE_DIR
Complete runtime state directory. Overrides
.BR XDG_STATE_HOME .
.TP
.B DS_INSTALL_DIR
Destination for the installed
.B ds
binary when running
.IR install.sh .
.TP
.B DS_LIB_DIR
Directory for bundled plugin installation and runtime discovery. The installer
default is
.IR ../lib/ds/plugins
relative to
.BR DS_INSTALL_DIR .
.TP
.B DS_MAN_DIR
Destination for installed manual pages. Defaults to
.IR ~/.local/share/man/man1 .
.SH TMUX RESURRECT INTEGRATION
The
.B resurrect save
command appends versioned ds session identity and shell metadata to the
tmux-resurrect snapshot supplied by its post-save-layout hook. It restricts the
snapshot to mode 0600.
.PP
The
.B resurrect begin
command marks the current tmux server restore as in progress so concurrent ds
callers do not create sessions while layouts are being rebuilt.
.PP
The
.B resurrect restore
command restores that metadata after tmux-resurrect finishes rebuilding the
environment.
When no file is given, it reads the
.I last
snapshot under the configured
.B @resurrect-dir .
Configure the plugin hooks as follows:
.PP
.nf
set -g @resurrect-hook-post-save-layout 'ds resurrect save'
set -g @resurrect-hook-pre-restore-all 'ds resurrect begin'
set -g @resurrect-hook-post-restore-all 'ds resurrect restore'
.fi
.PP
When the tmux-tools default-server coordinator disables continuum's native
restore, it publishes
.B @tmux-tools-resurrect-auto-restore
as
.BR on .
The
.B ds
command consumes that provider-owned tmux option to select the same startup
wait and halt-file behavior. The option is the complete integration boundary:
.B ds
does not invoke or otherwise require the
.B tmux-tools
executable.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The requested session operation succeeded.
.TP
.B 1
The requested session operation failed, or the command line was invalid.
